#: geonode/templates/help.html:52
#, python-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"          <p>The SDI provides access to data sets and a map editing "
"application allows users to browse existing maps and contribute their own.</"
"p>\n"
"  \n"
"          <h4 id=\"browsing-data\">Catalogue (Home) Page</h4>\n"
"          <p>The <a href=\"%(url_catalogue_browse)s\">Catalogue</a> page "
"allows you to browse data uploaded to this SDI.</p>\n"
"          <p>All data can be downloaded in a variety of formats, for use in "
"other applications.</p>\n"
"\n"
"          <h4 id=\"creating-a-layer\">Creating a Layer</h4>\n"
"          <p>SDI lets you to <a href=\"%(url_layer_upload)s\">upload spatial "
"data layers</a> in type of native formats: ESRI Shapefile (.shp, .shx, ."
"dbf, .xml and .prj)\n"
"            .kml .kmz; .geojson. See <a "
"href=\"%(url_layer_upload)s\">several tips before upload</a> and make sure "
"your layers are clean and the projection system is well defined.</p>\n"
"\n"
"          <h4 id=\"creating-a-dataset\">Creating a Dataset</h4>\n"
"          <p>SDI lets you to <a href=\"%(url_dataset_upload)s\">upload "
"multiple files</a> in variety of formats. All file types are supported for "
"upload and download in their original format. If you are uploading Tabular "
"Files (csv, tsv, sav, rdata, dta)\n"
"            SDI limits you to preview 1000 data in the dataset detail page.</"
"p>\n"
"  \n"
"          <h4 id=\"creating-a-map\">Creating a Map</h4>\n"
"          <p>To create a new map go to <a href=\"%(url_new_map)s\">this "
"link</a>.</p>\n"
"          <p>This will take you to the <a href=\"%(url_new_map)s\">Map "
"Composer</a> with a base layer loaded.</p>\n"
"          <p>To add data layers from the SDI click on the green plus button "
"located below the layers tab on the left hand side of the screen. This will "
"open a dialog listing all the layers available on the SDI.</p>\n"
"          <p>To add layers to your map select them and hit the <strong>Add "
"Spatial Data</strong> button. When finished you may hit <strong>Done</"
"strong> to close the dialog and go back to the map.</p>\n"
"  \n"
"          <h5>Reordering and Removing Layers</h5>\n"
"          <p>Change the display order of the layers listed in the data tab "
"by simply dragging and dropping their names. The order in the map will be "
"updated to reflect that. To turn a layer's visibility off simply uncheck it, "
"and to remove it entirely select it and hit the red minus button.</p>\n"
"  \n"
"          <h5>Saving your map</h5>\n"
"          <p>Once a suitable set of layers and zoom level has been found "
"it's time to save it so others can see it.  Click the Save button--the left "
"most icon on the top toolbar, an image of a map with a disk--on the top menu "
"and fill out the title and abstract of the map.</p>\n"
"  \n"
"          <h4 id=\"exporting-a-map\">Publishing a Map</h4>\n"
"          <p>Any map from the SDI can be embedded for use in another site or "
"blog. To publish a map:</p>\n"
"          <ol>\n"
"            <li>Select the from the list of maps on the community or map "
"page and then hit the 'Publish map' button.</li>\n"
"            <li>Choose your desired height and width for the widget in the "
"wizard.</li>\n"
"            <li>Copy the HTML snippet provided in the wizard to any HTML "
"page or iFrame-supporting blog post.</li>\n"
"          </ol>\n"
"          <p>This will put an interactive widget showing you map in your web "
"page or blog post.</p>\n"
"          <p>Note that the <a href=\"%(url_new_map)s\">Map Composer</a> also "
"has a button to publish the map. Just be sure to save the map before "
"publishing if there are changes that you want others to see. It publishes "
"the last saved version, not the last viewed version.</p>\n"
"  \n"
"          <h4 id=\"remixing-a-map\">Remixing a Map</h4>\n"
"          <p>Any map available can serve as a starting point for a new map.</"
"p>\n"
"          <ol>\n"
"            <li>Open the map in the Map Composer.</li>\n"
"            <li>Add and remove layers as you like.</li>\n"
"            <li>Pan and zoom to highlight the area of interest.</li>\n"
"            <li><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> Update the title, abstract, "
"contact info and tags to reflect the new map.</li>\n"
"            <li>Save the map.</li>\n"
"          </ol>\n"
"          <p>You will be able to see your new map when you search for it "
"from the <a href=\"%(url_catalogue_browse)s\">Catalogue</a> tab.</p>\n"
"          "
msgstr ""

